---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Food Supply Crisis Report"
  description="Privacy policy for Food Supply Crisis Report covering analytics, advertising, cookies, third-party services, external links and user choices."
  showAds={false}
>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: October 4, 2026.</strong></p>

    <p>Food Supply Crisis Report publishes evidence-led information about food supply, food prices, food security, climate, water, fertilizer, logistics and related topics. This policy explains what information may be processed when you use the site and the choices available to you.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>The site is a static publication and does not require an account or login to read articles. We do not ask readers to submit personal information merely to browse the publication. Information may be processed by third-party services that we use for analytics, hosting, security, advertising or communications.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics 4 is used to understand aggregate website usage, such as page views and general traffic patterns. Analytics is loaded only after you choose <strong>Allow analytics</strong> in the site's privacy choices control. If you decline analytics, the Google Analytics tag is not loaded.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics is a service provided by Google. Google may process information such as identifiers, device or browser information, approximate location and website interaction data according to its applicable terms and privacy practices. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>The site is currently in an AdSense-readiness phase. Google AdSense account verification is installed, but Google advertising tags are not currently being loaded on the public site. The site's previous third-party advertising scripts are also disabled during this compliance phase.</p>
    <p>When Google AdSense is enabled, Google and its advertising partners may use cookies, web beacons, IP addresses or similar technologies to help serve and measure advertising. Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</p>
    <p>Users may control personalized advertising through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>. Information about opting out of some third-party interest-based advertising is also available through <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YourAdChoices</a>.</p>
    <p>Before personalized Google advertising is enabled for users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the site will use an appropriate Google-certified consent management solution integrated with the applicable IAB Transparency and Consent Framework requirements. We will not treat this policy page itself as a substitute for that consent mechanism.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>The site uses browser storage to remember your analytics privacy choice. At present, the choice is stored locally in your browser under the site's own consent key. Other cookies or similar technologies may be set by third-party services only when those services are enabled. Your browser also provides controls for deleting or restricting cookies and local storage.</p>

    <h2>Advertising vendors and third parties</h2>
    <p>When advertising services are enabled, the specific advertising vendors and their relevant privacy information will be identified in this policy and, where applicable, in the site's consent experience. During the current compliance phase, third-party advertising delivery is disabled.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Articles and pages may link to government agencies, research organizations, news organizations and other external websites. Those websites operate under their own privacy policies, terms and data practices. We are not responsible for their practices.</p>

    <h2>Information you send us</h2>
    <p>If you contact us through the available correction or editorial enquiry channel, we may use the information you provide to review the request, respond to you and maintain an appropriate editorial record. Do not send passwords, financial account credentials or other highly sensitive personal information through an ordinary editorial request.</p>

    <h2>Your privacy choices</h2>
    <p>You can decline analytics when the privacy choices message appears. You can reopen the site's privacy choices control from the lower-right area of the page to change that analytics preference later.</p>
    <p>For Google advertising choices, use <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> when applicable. You may also use the privacy and cookie controls provided by your browser.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The publication is intended for a general audience and is not directed specifically at children. We do not knowingly request personal information from children through the site.</p>

    <h2>Data retention and security</h2>
    <p>Retention periods depend on the service involved and the purpose for which information was collected. We use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to a small static publication, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the site's analytics, advertising, consent, contact or data practices change. The latest version will be posted here with its update date.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
